.TH TUDUMD 1 "October 2026" "tudumd 0.10.5" "User Manuals"
.SH NAME
tudumd \- A command-line TUI tool to manage hierarchical TODO lists in Markdown format.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBtudumd\fR [\fB\-f\fR \fItudu_file\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig_file\fR] [\fB\-v[v]\fR] [\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBtudumd\fR is a Markdown-native fork of \fBTuDu\fR, a command-line ncurses TUI
tool to manage hierarchical TODO lists so that you can organize everything you
have to do in a simple and efficient way.
Instead of a database backend or opaque XML files, \fBtudumd\fR stores tasks in
human-readable plain \fBMarkdown (.md)\fR files (by default in
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/tudumd/tudu.md\fR, or \fI~/.local/share/tudumd/tudu.md\fR)
that can be viewed and edited directly in Markdown viewers and editors such as
\fBOkular\fR, \fBGhostwriter\fR, and \fBQuillpad\fR.

Every TODO task is composed of:
.TS
tab (>);
l l.
Status>Pending (\fB\- [ ]\fR) or Done (\fB\- [x]\fR).
Title>A short sentence summarizing the task.
Description text>A longer multi-line text providing more details. (Optional)
Priority>The urgency of the task (\fB1\fR\(en\fB5\fR, written as \fB!1\fR\(en\fB!5\fR). (Optional)
Category>One or more short tags such as \fB#home\fR, \fB#work\fR, \fB#inet\fR. (Optional)
Deadline>The latest date the task should be done (\fB@due(dd.mm.yyyy)\fR). (Optional)
Scheduled date>The planned date to do the task (\fB@sched(dd.mm.yyyy)\fR). (Optional)
Subtasks>Every task can have any number of nested subtasks. (Optional)
.TE

Tasks can be ordered by any of those fields, and categories can be used to filter
and display only specific kinds of tasks. \fBtudumd\fR also warns when a deadline is
approaching and displays the completion percentage of parent tasks.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP "\-f \fItudu_file\fP" 10
Load the given Markdown (or legacy TuDu XML) file instead of the default
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/tudumd/tudu.md\fR.
.IP "\-c \fIconfig_file\fP" 10
Load a specific configuration file.
.IP "\-v" 10
Display the \fBtudumd\fR version number.
.IP "\-vv" 10
Display license and copyright information.
.IP "\-h, \-\-help" 10
Display help and command-line usage.
.SH MARKDOWN FORMAT & LEGACY XML COMPATIBILITY
.PP
By default, \fBtudumd\fR reads and writes \fI~/.local/share/tudumd/tudu.md\fR
using standard 4-space-indented Markdown task lists:
.PP
.nf
.RS
- [ ] Prepare release notes !1 #work @due(20.10.2026) @sched(18.10.2026) [+]
    > First line of long description  
    > Second line of long description
    - [x] Verify package build
.RE
.fi
.PP
Multi-line descriptions are saved as indented blockquotes (\fB>\fR) with two
trailing spaces at the end of each non-final line so CommonMark/discount viewers
(\fBOkular\fR, \fBGhostwriter\fR, \fBQuillpad\fR) preserve line breaks inside
tight task lists without breaking list indentation. When reading manually edited
\fB.md\fR files, \fBtudumd\fR also accepts \fB<br>\fR, \fB<br/>\fR, and \fB<br />\fR
tags as line breaks.
.PP
\fBLegacy XML compatibility:\fR Although \fBtudumd\fR works natively with Markdown,
its parser automatically detects legacy TuDu XML files (starting with \fB<?xml\fR,
\fB<!DOCTYPE\fR, or \fB<todo\fR). If the XDG task file does not exist yet on first
launch and a legacy \fI~/.tudu.md\fR or \fI~/.tudu.xml\fR file is present,
\fBtudumd\fR imports it automatically and saves to
\fI~/.local/share/tudumd/tudu.md\fR. You can also convert between \fB.xml\fR and
\fB.md\fR in either direction offline using \fBtuduconvert\fR(1).
.PP
\fBSafe error handling:\fR If an existing \fB.md\fR or \fB.xml\fR file contains a
syntax error, \fBtudumd\fR reports the line number and exits with status 1 without
modifying or overwriting the user's file with the welcome template.
.SH INTERFACE
All the key bindings described here are the defaults in \fBtudumd\fR. They can be
customized in the configuration file.
.IP h
Move the cursor one level out in the tree depth.
.IP l
Move the cursor one level in in the tree depth.
.IP j
Move the cursor to the next task.
.IP k
Move the cursor to the previous task.
.IP J
Move a task one position down.
.IP K
Move a task one position up.
.IP m
Mark or unmark a task as done.
.IP dd
Delete a task (and copy it to the paste buffer).
.IP dt
Remove the deadline of the task.
.IP df
Remove the priority of the task.
.IP dS
Remove the scheduled date of the task.
.IP p
Paste the last deleted task under the current cursor line.
.IP P
Paste the last deleted task over the current cursor line.
.IP V
Paste the last deleted task as a subtask of the currently selected task.
.IP o
Add a new task below the cursor.
.IP O
Add a new task above the cursor.
.IP a
Edit the title of the task.
.IP t
Edit the deadline.
.IP f
Set the priority of the task (1\(en5).
.IP C
Add or modify the category of the task.
.IP e
Edit the long description text of the task.
.IP x
Scroll the text window upwards.
.IP z
Scroll the text window downwards.
.IP S
Edit the scheduled date of the task.
.IP X
Scroll the schedule window upwards.
.IP Z
Scroll the schedule window downwards.
.IP c
Collapse or expand the children of the current task.
.IP M
Hide or show tasks marked as done.
.IP /
Search for a pattern in task titles.
.IP n
Search the next occurrence of the last search.
.IP N
Search the previous occurrence of the last search.
.IP :
Open the command input. See the \fBCOMMANDS\fR section.
.IP bt
Sort by title.
.IP bT
Sort by title in reverse order.
.IP bd
Sort by done status.
.IP bD
Sort by done status in reverse order.
.IP bl
Sort by deadline.
.IP bL
Sort by deadline in reverse order.
.IP bp
Sort by priority.
.IP bP
Sort by priority in reverse order.
.IP bc
Sort by category.
.IP bC
Sort by category in reverse order.
.IP bu
Sort by user-defined order.
.IP bU
Sort by reversed user-defined order.
.IP s
Save all changes to disk (writing the previous version to \fI/tmp/tudu.md.bak\fR).
.IP ?
Display the built-in quick help screen.
.IP q
Quit \fBtudumd\fR saving the latest changes.
.IP Q
Quit \fBtudumd\fR without saving changes.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP "hide category1 category2 ... categoryN"
Hide one or more categories.
.IP "show category1 category2 ... categoryN"
Display one or more categories.
.IP showall
Display all categories.
.IP "showonly category1 category2 ... categoryN"
Hide all categories except the ones given.
.IP "help"
Display this manual page.
.SH CONFIG
The configuration file has several sections starting with a name in brackets,
such as \fB[ general ]\fR. Other configuration files can be included with:
.IP "@include = 'path'"

.PP
The options of each section are:

.SS general
.IP "collapse = yes|\fBno\fR"
Collapse tasks by default.
.IP "hide_done = yes|\fBno\fR"
Whether to hide tasks marked as done.
.IP "hide_percent = yes|\fBno\fR"
Whether to hide the completion percentage display on each parent task.
.IP "visual_tree = yes|\fBno\fR"
Toggle graphical tree markers such as \fB(+)\fR and \fB(\-)\fR to the left of parent tasks.
Useful in terminals where bold text is indistinguishable from normal text.
.IP "bold_parent = \fByes\fR|no"
Highlight parent tasks that have children using bold text.
.IP "loop_move = yes|\fBno\fR"
Whether to wrap around to the beginning (or end) when reaching the end (or beginning) of the list.
.IP "days_warn = number"
How many days before the task is due the deadline warning indicator is shown (default: 7).
.IP "us_dates = yes|\fBno\fR"
Use US date display format (\fBmm/dd/yyyy\fR) in the TUI instead of \fBdd/mm/yyyy\fR.
.IP "old_sched = \fByes\fR|no"
Whether to display past scheduled tasks in the scheduler pane using the warning color.
.IP "tudu_file = full-path"
Full path of the Markdown TODO file to load when no \fB\-f\fR argument is given.
If not set, \fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/tudumd/tudu.md\fR (default
\fI~/.local/share/tudumd/tudu.md\fR) is used.
.IP "sort_order = string"
Default order in which tasks are displayed. Tasks are ordered by the 1st letter
in the string, then by the 2nd, and so on:
.RS
.IP t
title (\fBT\fR for reverse)
.IP d
done status (\fBD\fR for reverse)
.IP l
deadline (\fBL\fR for reverse)
.IP p
priority (\fBP\fR for reverse)
.IP c
category (\fBC\fR for reverse)
.IP e
percentage done (\fBE\fR for reverse)
.IP u
user-defined order (\fBU\fR for reverse)
.RE
.IP "editor = 'path_bin %s'"
Optional external editor command used when editing long task descriptions with \fBe\fR.
.SS keys
Defines custom key bindings for the program. See \fI/etc/tudumdrc\fR for examples.
.SS theme
Window positions are described by rows using the syntax:
.RS
row = [height]([width|]window[, [width|]window, ...])
.RE
The height and width can be a character count or a percentage followed by
\fB%\fR. Possible windows are: \fBhelp\fR, \fBtree\fR, \fBinfo\fR, \fBblank\fR,
\fBvpipe\fR, \fBhpipe\fR, \fBtext\fR, and \fBschedule\fR.

Other theme options:
.IP "columns = colm1,...,colmN"
Columns in the tree window: \fBtitle\fR, \fBpriority\fR, \fBcategory\fR, \fBdeadline\fR.
.IP "category_length = numChar"
Number of characters displayed for the category column.
.IP "color = color_text, color_background"
Default text and background colors: \fBblack\fR, \fBred\fR, \fBgreen\fR, \fByellow\fR,
\fBblue\fR, \fBmagenta\fR, \fBcyan\fR, \fBwhite\fR, \fBtransparent\fR, or \fB(r, g, b)\fR
with values from 0 to 1000.
.IP "window = color_text, color_background"
Per-window color overrides (\fBpipe\fR sets both \fBvpipe\fR and \fBhpipe\fR).
.IP "selected = color_text, color_background"
Colors for the currently highlighted cursor line.
.IP "warn = color_text, color_background"
Colors for approaching deadlines and overdue scheduled tasks.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP "\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR"
Base directory for user configuration files. If unset, defaults to \fI~/.config\fR
(so user configuration is read from \fI~/.config/tudumd/tudumdrc\fR).
.IP "\fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR"
Base directory for user data files. If unset, defaults to \fI~/.local/share\fR
(so the default TODO list is stored in \fI~/.local/share/tudumd/tudu.md\fR).
.SH FILES
.SS Configuration & User Data Files (XDG Base Directory Specification)
.IP "\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tudumd/tudumdrc\fR (default: \fI~/.config/tudumd/tudumdrc\fR)"
Primary user configuration file. (Legacy \fI~/.tudumdrc\fR and \fI~/.tudurc\fR are
also read as lower-priority fallbacks if they already exist.)
.IP "\fI/etc/tudumdrc\fR (fallback: \fI/etc/tudurc\fR)"
Global system-wide configuration file.
.IP "\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/tudumd/tudu.md\fR (default: \fI~/.local/share/tudumd/tudu.md\fR)"
Default user TODO list file in Markdown format. Its parent directory is created
automatically on first run so no files are placed in the root of \fI~\fR.
.IP "\fI/usr/share/tudumd/welcome.md\fR"
Default welcome template loaded when creating a new TODO file for the first time.
.SS Runtime, Lock & Backup Service Files
.IP "\fI~/.local/share/tudumd/.tudu.md_lock\fR (or \fI.<filename>_lock\fR)"
Session lock file created in the same directory as the opened TODO file while
\fBtudumd\fR is running to prevent concurrent modifications. Automatically deleted
when \fBtudumd\fR exits normally.
.IP "\fI/tmp/tudu.md.bak\fR"
Single rolling backup file. Before each save operation (\fBs\fR or \fBq\fR),
\fBtudumd\fR copies the previous contents of the TODO file to \fI/tmp/tudu.md.bak\fR
so working directories are never cluttered with per-file \fI.bak\fR files.
.IP "\fI/tmp/tudu.XXXXXX\fR"
Temporary file created only when an external text editor (\fBeditor =\fR in config)
is invoked to edit a task's long description; deleted immediately after the editor exits.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tuduconvert (1)
